## DESCRIPTION
##   Working with Vectors
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## Tagged by nhamblet

## DBsubject(Geometry)
## DBchapter(Vector geometry)
## DBsection(Dot product, length, and unit vectors)
## Date(8/23/07)
## Institution(Union College)
## MLT(ProjectionsComponentNotation)
## Level(3)
## MO(1)
## TitleText1('Calculus')
## AuthorText1('Anton')
## EditionText1('7')
## Section1('12.3')
## Problem1('22')
## KEYWORDS('Vector', 'Projection', 'Orthogonal')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'parserVectorUtils.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context("Vector");

$U = non_zero_vector3D();
$V = non_zero_vector3D();

#  The projections
$U1 = Compute("(($U.$V)/($V.$V)) * $V");
$U2 = Compute("$U - $U1");

BEGIN_PGML

Suppose [`\vec{u} = [$U]`] and [`\vec{v} = [$V]`].  Then:

a) The vector projection of [`\vec{u}`] along [`\vec{v}`] is [_]{$U1}{40}.  

b) The vector projection of [`\vec{u}`] orthogonal to [`\vec{v}`] is [_]{$U2}{40}.

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
a) Let [``\vec{w} = \frac{\vec{v}}{\sqrt{\vec{v} \cdot \vec{v}}}``] be the unit vector that points in the same direction as [`\vec{u}`].  The _scalar projection_ of [`\vec{u}`] along [`\vec{v}`] is the dot product [``\vec{u}\cdot \vec{w} = \frac{\vec{u}\cdot \vec{v}}{\sqrt{\vec{v} \cdot \vec{v}}}``].  The _vector projection_ of [`\vec{u}`] along [`\vec{v}`] is the scalar projection times times [`\vec{w}`]:    

        [```\text{proj}_{\vec{v}}(\vec{u}) =  \frac{\vec{u}\cdot \vec{v}}{\sqrt{\vec{v} \cdot \vec{v}}}\frac{\vec{v}}{\sqrt{\vec{v} \cdot \vec{v}}}= \frac{\vec{u}\cdot \vec{v}}{\vec{v} \cdot \vec{v}}\vec{v} = \frac{[@ $U.$V @]}{ [@ $V.$V @] }[$V]```]

b) [`\vec{v}`] is the sum of two perpendicular vectors, one points in the same direction as [`\vec{u}`], and the other points in a direction perpendicular to [`\vec{u}`].  The first is [``\text{proj}_{\vec{v}}(\vec{u})``], the vector from part a). The other, [``\vec{v}-\text{proj}_{\vec{v}}(\vec{u})``], is the vector that's requested in part b).  So the answer for part b) is    

        [``[$U] - \frac{[@ $U.$V @]}{ [@ $V.$V @] }[$V]``]    
END_PGML_SOLUTION

#  Answers

#ANS($U1->cmp);
#ANS($U2->cmp);

ENDDOCUMENT();
